`promptAiSetup` returns `true` when `skipPrompt` is `true`. `skipPrompt` is set to `true` whenever `--yes` is passed or the terminal is non-interactive. This means `storybook init --yes` — the standard flag used in CI/CD pipelines and automation scripts — will silently add `@storybook/addon-mcp` to every project without any user consent. The default for a skipped opt-in prompt should be `false`, not `true`:
```ts
if (skipPrompt) {
  return false;
}
```
